Account: none beyond an email address. The NASA Exoplanet Archive takes messages through its help desk form ({{ f.helpdesk_url }}). The engine cannot send it.

When: after the Research Note is published, since the archive adds objects from the literature. Paste this paragraph (also in `archive_email.txt`), with the two DOIs filled in:

> {{ archive_paragraph }}

## Step 5. {{ titles["5"] }}

Account: whatever the person asks through (ExoFOP messages, email). The engine cannot reply for you.

Observers who plan a transit ask for the ephemeris first. Send `data/ephemeris.csv` and say: mid-transit times are T = {{ n.t0_bjd }} + E x {{ n.period }} (BJD_TDB, E a whole number of orbits), the transit lasts {{ n.duration }} h, and the dossier carries no formal error on the period or the first mid-transit (the box search does not give one), so a window of at least one transit duration either side of each predicted time is needed, more for times years after 2013. Send `data/lightcurve.csv` and `data/events.csv` to anyone checking the depth, and `dossier.html` to anyone who wants the full vetting. Point every request at the Zenodo DOI, so everyone works from the same frozen files.

